{"id": "Mercury_175385", "question": "What happens to a wooden log when it is burned?", "step_idx": 1, "options": ["A): It is completely destroyed.", "B): It is completely changed into heat energy.", "C): It changes into other types of matter and energy.", "D): It physically changes into the gaseous phase."], "correct": "C", "initial_cot": "1. When a wooden log is burned, it undergoes a chemical reaction called combustion.\n2. During combustion, the wood reacts with oxygen in the air, breaking down the complex organic molecules in the wood into simpler molecules.\n3. This process releases energy in the form of heat and light.\n4. The wood is not completely destroyed, as some of its components are transformed into other types of matter (such as ash, carbon dioxide, and water vapor).\n5. The energy released during combustion is not completely converted into heat energy, as some of it is also released as light energy.\n6. The wood does not physically change into the gaseous phase; instead, it breaks down into gaseous byproducts.", "initial_cot_probs": [2.375006999955076e-07, 2.375006999955076e-07, 0.00010857219604076818, 3.2142224881681614e-08], "initial_probs": [6.736423529218882e-06, 1.426100789103657e-05, 0.000687133870087564, 7.633368113602046e-06], "prediction": 2, "cot_prediction": 2, "adapter_id": "Mercury_175385_step_1", "global_job_index": 139, "cot_step": "When a wooden log is burned, it undergoes a chemical reaction called combustion.", "segmented_cot": ["1.", "When a wooden log is burned, it undergoes a chemical reaction called combustion.", "2.", "During combustion, the wood reacts with oxygen in the air, breaking down the complex organic molecules in the wood into simpler molecules.", "3.", "This process releases energy in the form of heat and light.", "4.", "The wood is not completely destroyed, as some of its components are transformed into other types of matter (such as ash, carbon dioxide, and water vapor).", "5.", "The energy released during combustion is not completely converted into heat energy, as some of it is also released as light energy.", "6.", "The wood does not physically change into the gaseous phase; instead, it breaks down into gaseous byproducts."], "causal_cot": {"loss": "frodo_reasoning_module", "answer_source": "correct", "counterfactual": "remove_step", "lambda": 0.1, "margin": 1.0, "ie_lambda": 1.0, "margin_lambda": 1.0, "auto_scale": true}, "adapter_record": {"base_model_id": "microsoft/Phi-3-mini-4k-instruct", "adapter_id": "Mercury_175385_step_1", "adapter_path": "../../../../adapters/arc-challenge/Phi-3/npo_KL_sentencize_s=True_lr=0.0005_rs=1001_pos=True_ff2=False_critical_lora_causal_cot_i09_unfiltered_pos_s1/Mercury_175385_step_1.pt", "metadata": {"base_model_id": "microsoft/Phi-3-mini-4k-instruct", "dataset": "arc-challenge", "strategy": "sentencize", "stepwise": true, "method": "npo_KL", "instance_id": "Mercury_175385", "step_idx": 1, "target_index": 19, "global_job_index": 139, "question": "What happens to a wooden log when it is burned?", "causal_cot": {"loss": "frodo_reasoning_module", "answer_source": "correct", "counterfactual": "remove_step", "lambda": 0.1, "margin": 1.0, "ie_lambda": 1.0, "margin_lambda": 1.0, "auto_scale": true}}}, "adapter_record_path": "v2_outputs/adapter_records/arc-challenge/Phi-3/npo_KL_sentencize_s=True_lr=0.0005_rs=1001_pos=True_ff2=False_critical_lora_causal_cot_i09_unfiltered_pos_s1/Mercury_175385_step_1.json", "adapter_training_history": [{"epoch": 1, "mean_loss": 15.249238014221191, "evaluation": null}, {"epoch": 2, "mean_loss": 9.606377601623535, "evaluation": null}, {"epoch": 3, "mean_loss": 1.485762119293213, "evaluation": null}, {"epoch": 4, "mean_loss": 0.3404790461063385, "evaluation": null}, {"epoch": 5, "mean_loss": 0.21435846388339996, "evaluation": {"completion": "C ) It changes into other types of matter and", "probs": [0.0042408425360918045, 0.006991967558860779, 0.6293968558311462, 0.024404363706707954], "prediction": 2, "target_cot_ste