's rotation.\n5. As the Sun moves, the angle at which its light reaches the student changes.\n6. When the Sun is directly overhead, the light will hit the student at a 90-degree angle.\n7. This means that the student's body will cast a shadow directly underneath her.\n8. The length of the shadow depends on the angle of the Sun's light and the height of the student.\n9. The shorter the angle, the shorter the shadow will be.\n10. The Sun's position in the sky changes throughout the day, so we need to consider the different times mentioned in the question.", "new_cot_probs": [1.871481981652323e-05, 6.403859060810646e-07, 5.651386345562059e-07, 4.175840786047047e-06], "cot_prob": [-1.7243009805679321], "cot_step_prob": [-3.6816251277923584], "mechanistic_diagnostics": {"prompt_lengths": {"answer_prompt_tokens": 206, "removed_answer_prompt_tokens": 185, "step_token_count": 23}, "representation": {"step_answer_cosine_by_layer": [0.04406151548027992, 0.8653489947319031, 0.7797049283981323, 0.7555116415023804, 0.7194902300834656, 0.710070013999939, 0.6671758890151978, 0.6568858623504639, 0.6663400530815125, 0.6423509120941162, 0.6360160112380981, 0.6420645117759705, 0.6196122169494629, 0.6117803454399109, 0.6136680841445923, 0.5696175694465637, 0.5694221258163452, 0.5756245255470276, 0.5632380843162537, 0.612568199634552, 0.6063897013664246, 0.5909549593925476, 0.5831408500671387, 0.5986928939819336, 0.5969083905220032, 0.6470409035682678, 0.6669501662254333, 0.6571547389030457, 0.7124715447425842, 0.746705949306488, 0.7631689310073853, 0.7946473956108093, 0.6164642572402954], "answer_removed_cosine_by_layer": [1.0, 0.9999468326568604, 0.999836802482605, 0.9997619390487671, 0.9996860027313232, 0.9993902444839478, 0.9993012547492981, 0.9990377426147461, 0.9988013505935669, 0.9986287355422974, 0.9982776045799255, 0.9981720447540283, 0.9981681108474731, 0.9979934096336365, 0.9969996213912964, 0.9950281977653503, 0.9922364950180054, 0.9898078441619873, 0.9881088733673096, 0.990