ts of the Sun, Moon, and Earth.\n3. The Sun should be the central ball, as it is the largest and most important object in this scenario.\n4. The Earth should be a smaller ball, as it is much smaller than the Sun and the Moon.\n5. The Moon should be an even smaller ball, as it is smaller than both the Sun and the Earth.\n6. The Moon should be able to move around the Earth, as it orbits the Earth in real life.\n7. The Sun should be able to shine light on the Earth, as it emits light and heat.", "new_cot_probs": [2.7449177650851198e-05, 4.676296327943419e-08, 2.503040796852929e-08, 3.8385374878657785e-09], "cot_prob": [-0.43014538288116455], "cot_step_prob": [-0.1696784645318985], "mechanistic_diagnostics": {"prompt_lengths": {"answer_prompt_tokens": 333, "removed_answer_prompt_tokens": 314, "step_token_count": 26}, "representation": {"step_answer_cosine_by_layer": [0.03224417567253113, 0.8588461875915527, 0.7703614234924316, 0.741938591003418, 0.6975997686386108, 0.6735487580299377, 0.6280476450920105, 0.601926863193512, 0.6185175180435181, 0.5945932865142822, 0.5893096923828125, 0.5968096256256104, 0.584938645362854, 0.5747663974761963, 0.5970205664634705, 0.5492459535598755, 0.5480417013168335, 0.5534892082214355, 0.5666477084159851, 0.6187267303466797, 0.5925682187080383, 0.5987052321434021, 0.5983090400695801, 0.6213552951812744, 0.6146931648254395, 0.6636552810668945, 0.6954324245452881, 0.7072924375534058, 0.7640407085418701, 0.7901638150215149, 0.8116437196731567, 0.8366042375564575, 0.6868420839309692], "answer_removed_cosine_by_layer": [1.0, 0.9999382495880127, 0.9999048709869385, 0.9997071027755737, 0.9996521472930908, 0.9993788003921509, 0.9993888139724731, 0.9993324875831604, 0.9991765022277832, 0.9991434812545776, 0.9987934827804565, 0.9987004995346069, 0.9976543188095093, 0.9975956082344055, 0.9976907968521118, 0.9974110126495361, 0.9972738027572632, 0.9966520071029663, 0.9966170787811279, 0.9966270923614502, 0.995964765548706, 0.9959765076637268, 0.9963