ity, and it will start to collapse.\n3. As the core collapses, the core's density and gravity increase because the core's mass remains the same while its volume decreases.\n4. The core's increasing density and gravity cause the core to heat up as the particles are compressed closer together.\n5. The core's temperature eventually becomes high enough to start fusing helium into heavier elements (like carbon and oxygen).\n6. The core's core is now a helium core, and the core's core is now hotter and denser than it was when it was fusing hydrogen.\n7. The core's core is now hotter and denser than it was when it was fusing hydrogen.\n8. The core's core is now hotter and denser than it was when it was fusing hydrogen.\n9. The core's core is now hotter and denser than it was when it was fusing hydrogen.\n10. The core's core is now hotter and denser than it was when it was fusing hydrogen.\n11. The core's core is now hot", "new_cot_probs": [2.707053499761969e-05, 2.2220847313292325e-06, 0.0014780010096728802, 5.3305038818507455e-06], "cot_prob": [-1.9048570394515991], "cot_step_prob": [-5.719930171966553], "mechanistic_diagnostics": {"prompt_lengths": {"answer_prompt_tokens": 200, "removed_answer_prompt_tokens": 181, "step_token_count": 21}, "representation": {"step_answer_cosine_by_layer": [0.05662771686911583, 0.870026707649231, 0.7928252816200256, 0.7656218409538269, 0.7224024534225464, 0.7128008008003235, 0.6647350192070007, 0.6487361788749695, 0.6685364246368408, 0.653109610080719, 0.6433306336402893, 0.6540642380714417, 0.640135645866394, 0.6213254332542419, 0.6344415545463562, 0.5882631540298462, 0.5872684717178345, 0.5997992157936096, 0.6191777586936951, 0.6684579253196716, 0.6563680171966553, 0.6574420928955078, 0.6556130051612854, 0.6893994808197021, 0.6954583525657654, 0.7396025657653809, 0.762814462184906, 0.7608492374420166, 0.7989120483398438, 0.804349422454834, 0.8234037756919861, 0.8442223072052002, 0.7972335815429688], "answer_removed_cosine_by_layer": [1.0