67e-06], [3.466185080469586e-05, 3.058897709706798e-05, 0.00848147552460432, 4.4506698031909764e-05], [0.001161051681265235, 1.2898119166493416e-05, 1.3594517440651543e-06, 4.4134932863926224e-07], [1.9982595404144377e-05, 0.001236279378645122, 0.007114296779036522, 0.00016731221694499254], [0.0031481583137065172, 7.8035036494839e-06, 1.5366010757134063e-06, 7.8035036494839e-06], [0.00015093243564479053, 4.900058775092475e-05, 0.003031559055671096, 2.0426483388291672e-05], [0.0030468173790723085, 5.58044011995662e-05, 9.20059101190418e-05, 1.811703623388894e-05], [6.881884928588988e-06, 3.6836074741586344e-06, 0.0051869056187570095, 1.2857053661718965e-05], [5.160919317859225e-05, 0.0008073035860434175, 0.00765948323532939, 4.019328116555698e-05], [0.0046610152348876, 0.00018072717648465186, 8.536947279935703e-05, 0.0002979687415063381], [0.0026151826605200768, 0.001235324889421463, 0.0009620719938538969, 0.0007492623990401626], [0.00047967981663532555, 0.003544381121173501, 0.002149775857105851, 0.00047967981663532555], [1.608647289685905e-05, 4.372756666271016e-05, 0.008332999423146248, 0.0002516347449272871], [0.00657349918037653, 9.37659278861247e-05, 1.6294075976475142e-05, 3.449455834925175e-05], [1.5365421859314665e-06, 1.2865309145126957e-05, 1.5365421859314665e-06, 0.005190236493945122], [0.0038762667682021856, 3.353627835167572e-05, 0.0001929879654198885, 1.2337307452980895e-05], [3.489806113066152e-05, 0.004033667501062155, 3.678228495118674e-06, 7.786808964738157e-06], [0.0040266746655106544, 1.4522455785481725e-05, 4.160753633186687e-06, 1.7344601701552165e-06], [9.22961626201868e-05, 0.00019539098138920963, 8.584880561102182e-06, 0.008308235555887222], [5.350433184503345e-06, 0.00403264444321394, 8.821373739920091e-06, 2.1161375116207637e-05]], "new_cot": "1. We know that when two objects are rubbed together, they can become electrically charged due to the transfer of electrons. This is known as the triboelectric effect.\n2. The type of charge (positiv