 soil fertility and thus crop productivity.\n4. Leaching of soils (A) would generally decrease productivity by washing away nutrients.\n5. Evaporation rates (B) could affect productivity, but they would likely have a more uniform effect across the valley, not just in certain areas.\n6. Amounts of sunlight (D) could also affect productivity, but again, this would likely be more consistent across the valley.", "new_cot_probs": [7.803864718880504e-06, 4.177108166913968e-06, 0.0031483040656894445, 1.4579539310943801e-05], "cot_prob": [-0.9106808304786682], "cot_step_prob": [-5.59721565246582], "mechanistic_diagnostics": {"prompt_lengths": {"answer_prompt_tokens": 392, "removed_answer_prompt_tokens": 389, "step_token_count": 16}, "representation": {"step_answer_cosine_by_layer": [-0.013750034384429455, 0.846052348613739, 0.7642722725868225, 0.7373274564743042, 0.706271231174469, 0.7003453373908997, 0.6618725657463074, 0.6653024554252625, 0.7104771137237549, 0.7157988548278809, 0.7235121130943298, 0.7190823554992676, 0.6851068735122681, 0.6779243350028992, 0.6851905584335327, 0.637184202671051, 0.6268177032470703, 0.6509444713592529, 0.6461606025695801, 0.6975266337394714, 0.6611621379852295, 0.6598643660545349, 0.6583922505378723, 0.694574773311615, 0.714143693447113, 0.7668126225471497, 0.7821291089057922, 0.7703649997711182, 0.8029972910881042, 0.8002030849456787, 0.8151840567588806, 0.831745445728302, 0.8433705568313599], "answer_removed_cosine_by_layer": [1.0, 0.9999538064002991, 0.9998974800109863, 0.9997699856758118, 0.9996938705444336, 0.9994573593139648, 0.9992870092391968, 0.9989719390869141, 0.9987607002258301, 0.9988390207290649, 0.998843789100647, 0.9988535642623901, 0.999025285243988, 0.9986782670021057, 0.9986078143119812, 0.9982452988624573, 0.9982160329818726, 0.9981151819229126, 0.9977047443389893, 0.99784916639328, 0.9976913332939148, 0.9976208806037903, 0.995577871799469, 0.9965090751647949, 0.9967259168624878, 0.9973052740097046, 0.9972522258758545, 0