7372e-07, 1.0445887710375246e-08, 7.469799311365932e-05], [7.267179898917675e-05, 4.32122249094391e-07, 2.486691982994671e-06, 1.238050941765323e-07], [6.426076311072393e-07, 9.537142614135519e-05, 5.2748447387784836e-08, 1.1166846292098853e-07], [7.462781650247052e-05, 1.6324767670994333e-07, 3.642547952154018e-08, 9.209803586429643e-09], [6.995775265750126e-07, 3.552747557478142e-06, 5.067722597118518e-08, 4.3281328544253483e-05], [3.20653228413903e-08, 4.5151336962589994e-05, 5.286678117499832e-08, 1.1191897186790811e-07]], "new_cot": "1. We are given that both samples have the same volume, which is one liter.\n2. We know that the density of a substance is the mass per unit volume.\n3. We are given the densities of both substances: the density of the feathers is 0.0025 g/cm\u00b3 and the density of the nails is 7.8 g/cm\u00b3.\n4. We can use the formula for density (density = mass/volume) to find the mass of each sample.\n5. Since the volume is the same for both samples (1 liter = 1000 cm\u00b3), we can rearrange the formula to find the mass (mass = density * volume).\n6. Calculating the mass for each sample:\n   - Mass of feathers = 0.0025 g/cm\u00b3 * 1000 cm\u00b3 = 2.5 g\n   - Mass of nails = 7.8 g/cm\u00b3 * 1000 cm\u00b3 = 7800 g\n7. Comparing the masses, we see that the mass of the nails (7800 g) is much greater than the mass of the feathers (2.5 g).", "new_cot_probs": [1.7390859738952713e-06, 1.7390859738952713e-06, 0.0004255402891431004, 1.1952550948990392e-06], "cot_prob": [-1.0022627115249634], "cot_step_prob": [-5.90810489654541], "mechanistic_diagnostics": {"prompt_lengths": {"answer_prompt_tokens": 258, "removed_answer_prompt_tokens": 255, "step_token_count": 10}, "representation": {"step_answer_cosine_by_layer": [0.030750542879104614, 0.8305898308753967, 0.7572686076164246, 0.7237411737442017, 0.6878814101219177, 0.6867245435714722, 0.6410133242607117, 0.628582239151001, 0.6532542705535889, 0.6325262188911438, 0.6207326650619507, 0.6320419907569885