{"id": "TIMSS_2007_8_pg109", "question": "Which of the following is the best way to determine whether two people are related?", "step_idx": 5, "options": ["A): Compare their blood types.", "B): Compare their handwriting.", "C): Compare their genes.", "D): Compare their fingerprints."], "correct": "C", "initial_cot": "1. Determining if two people are related involves finding a genetic connection between them.\n2. Blood types can provide some information about genetic relationships, but they are not specific enough to determine if two people are related.\n3. Handwriting and fingerprints are unique to individuals and do not provide any information about genetic relationships.\n4. Comparing genes is the most accurate way to determine if two people are related, as it directly examines their genetic makeup.", "initial_cot_probs": [3.220600319764344e-08, 3.846458263012664e-09, 2.7505819161888212e-05, 1.0455758037153373e-08], "initial_probs": [4.5467226300388575e-05, 2.9066225124552147e-06, 0.00023090161266736686, 4.22911125497194e-06], "prediction": 2, "cot_prediction": 2, "adapter_id": "TIMSS_2007_8_pg109_step_5", "global_job_index": 1449, "cot_step": "Handwriting and fingerprints are unique to individuals and do not provide any information about genetic relationships.", "segmented_cot": ["1.", "Determining if two people are related involves finding a genetic connection between them.", "2.", "Blood types can provide some information about genetic relationships, but they are not specific enough to determine if two people are related.", "3.", "Handwriting and fingerprints are unique to individuals and do not provide any information about genetic relationships.", "4.", "Comparing genes is the most accurate way to determine if two people are related, as it directly examines their genetic makeup."], "causal_cot": {"loss": "frodo_reasoning_module", "answer_source": "correct", "counterfactual": "remove_step", "lambda": 0.1, "margin": 1.0, "ie_lambda": 1.0, "margin_lambda": 1.0, 