gative charge after being rubbed with a piece of fur?\n\nChoices:\n(A): The fur gives up protons to the rod.\n(B): The rod gives up electrons to the air.\n(C): The fur gains protons from the rod.\n(D): The rod gains electrons from the fur.\n\nAssistant: Let's think step by step:\n\n1.\nWhen a plastic rod is rubbed with a piece of fur, electrons are transferred between the two materials.\n2.\nThe fur tends to lose electrons, which are negatively charged particles.\n3.", "specificity_preds": [1, 2, 0, 2, 0, 2, 0, 2, 2, 0, 0, 1, 2, 0, 3, 0, 1, 0, 3, 1], "specificity_probs": [[9.909324035106692e-06, 0.013953367248177528, 1.4417981219594367e-05, 9.909324035106692e-06], [0.00015020748833194375, 0.00013255765952635556, 0.03675456345081329, 0.000192870240425691], [0.005190419964492321, 2.7236825189902447e-05, 5.363248419598676e-06, 2.235734655187116e-06], [7.164681301219389e-05, 0.00502282939851284, 0.01365346647799015, 0.0004122989485040307], [0.008509060367941856, 2.7082474844064564e-05, 8.792391781753395e-06, 3.477458449197002e-05], [0.00025020402972586453, 0.00025020402972586453, 0.01063894759863615, 4.926810288452543e-05], [0.005062927026301622, 7.221877604024485e-05, 0.00011906862346222624, 4.3802901927847415e-05], [1.1285551408946048e-05, 1.2788204912794754e-05, 0.010921879671514034, 2.108418630086817e-05], [3.9193306292872876e-05, 0.0031135098543018103, 0.00846339762210846, 5.7025925343623385e-05], [0.008167615160346031, 0.00019208389858249575, 0.00011650477244984359, 0.0003166928072459996], [0.005673659034073353, 0.004418649710714817, 0.0026800467167049646, 0.0026800467167049646], [0.0006077787838876247, 0.009507259353995323, 0.004490911494940519, 0.0006077787838876247], [2.011406104429625e-05, 0.0001486239198129624, 0.017178591340780258, 0.0010981904342770576], [0.010725515894591808, 0.0002522399299778044, 2.0705116185126826e-05, 4.383273335406557e-05], [4.198132228339091e-05, 0.00024158581800293177, 5.390508522395976e-05, 0.05911410227417946], [0.0062265167944133