id point, as peer review helps ensure that the conclusions drawn from the data are accurate and supported by evidence.\n- Option (C) claims that it deters other scientists from duplicating research. While peer review does help prevent duplication, it's not the primary reason for presenting results for review.\n- Option (D) says it ensures that researchers receive credit. While credit is important, the main purpose of presenting results for review is to validate the findings and ensure their accuracy.", "new_cot_probs": [1.343071698300946e-08, 1.6689655240043066e-05, 2.6446651535394494e-09, 7.188944994851454e-09], "cot_prob": [-0.39035215973854065], "cot_step_prob": [-0.743256151676178], "mechanistic_diagnostics": {"prompt_lengths": {"answer_prompt_tokens": 288, "removed_answer_prompt_tokens": 278, "step_token_count": 15}, "representation": {"step_answer_cosine_by_layer": [0.20020495355129242, 0.8747138381004333, 0.7971506714820862, 0.7888977527618408, 0.7536908984184265, 0.7466846704483032, 0.7048818469047546, 0.7071936130523682, 0.7257174253463745, 0.7306292653083801, 0.7231494784355164, 0.7230449914932251, 0.7107412815093994, 0.6843799352645874, 0.7101662158966064, 0.6744045615196228, 0.6914105415344238, 0.697001576423645, 0.6968046426773071, 0.7382304668426514, 0.7289401292800903, 0.7189500331878662, 0.72332763671875, 0.731413722038269, 0.7349966764450073, 0.7803101539611816, 0.7904582023620605, 0.7852931022644043, 0.8226896524429321, 0.8377566933631897, 0.8554552793502808, 0.870700478553772, 0.6295337677001953], "answer_removed_cosine_by_layer": [1.0, 0.9999509453773499, 0.999893069267273, 0.99971604347229, 0.9996927380561829, 0.9995755553245544, 0.9993866682052612, 0.9993571043014526, 0.9988127946853638, 0.9987912774085999, 0.9984639286994934, 0.9983545541763306, 0.9985257387161255, 0.9976605772972107, 0.9971851110458374, 0.9953086376190186, 0.9921308755874634, 0.984891951084137, 0.9794294834136963, 0.9790478944778442, 0.9741547107696533, 0.9757297039031982, 0.