86437368106937e-10, 8.300756917378749e-07, 6.6798933051615e-10, 1.4141333659623001e-09]], "new_cot": "1. The question describes a scenario where an algae bloom occurs due to nutrient-rich runoff from heavy rains.\n2. Algae blooms can lead to a process called eutrophication, where the algae consume a lot of nutrients and proliferate rapidly.\n3. When the algae die, their decomposition by bacteria consumes oxygen from the water, leading to a decrease in dissolved oxygen levels.\n4. Aquatic organisms, especially those that are bottom dwellers or have limited mobility, require oxygen to survive.\n5. A significant reduction in oxygen levels can lead to hypoxic conditions, which are harmful to marine life.\n6. In such conditions, fish and other mobile organisms may leave the area in search of better-oxygenated waters.\n7. Bottom dwellers, which are less mobile and cannot easily escape, are at a higher risk of dying due to the lack of oxygen.", "new_cot_probs": [2.787878261578669e-10, 7.578238037098117e-10, 4.0563385983460876e-10, 3.72452905139653e-06], "cot_prob": [-1.5294756889343262], "cot_step_prob": [-2.129039764404297], "mechanistic_diagnostics": {"prompt_lengths": {"answer_prompt_tokens": 239, "removed_answer_prompt_tokens": 221, "step_token_count": 20}, "representation": {"step_answer_cosine_by_layer": [0.009075669571757317, 0.8546434044837952, 0.6906183958053589, 0.3893906772136688, 0.36623719334602356, 0.4253195524215698, 0.43209055066108704, 0.4491676390171051, 0.6246013641357422, 0.6067624688148499, 0.6026725769042969, 0.6252051591873169, 0.6137941479682922, 0.6043617725372314, 0.6171387434005737, 0.571459949016571, 0.5690210461616516, 0.540144145488739, 0.5532009601593018, 0.6076402068138123, 0.5957330465316772, 0.6089681386947632, 0.5920579433441162, 0.6424545645713806, 0.6695481538772583, 0.723026692867279, 0.7499372959136963, 0.7501813173294067, 0.7916094660758972, 0.8059649467468262, 0.829409122467041, 0.8522324562072754, 0.7311633229255676], "answer_remov