ermal reservoirs.\n4. To harness this energy, we need a source of heat, which is provided by hot rock (A).\n5. Fossil fuels (B) are not necessary for geothermal energy production, as they are a separate energy source.\n6. A thick crust (C) may provide insulation, but it is not the primary factor in geothermal energy production.\n7. Warm climate (D) is not directly related to geothermal energy production, as it depends on the heat from the Earth's core.", "new_cot_probs": [8.938783139456064e-06, 3.160530448464982e-10, 1.4929288361109627e-10, 1.7830492290982214e-11], "cot_prob": [-0.42826181650161743], "cot_step_prob": [-0.41123998165130615], "mechanistic_diagnostics": {"prompt_lengths": {"answer_prompt_tokens": 283, "removed_answer_prompt_tokens": 262, "step_token_count": 27}, "representation": {"step_answer_cosine_by_layer": [0.17355670034885406, 0.8764498233795166, 0.7907251715660095, 0.7482824325561523, 0.6990624070167542, 0.693788468837738, 0.6378520727157593, 0.6364423632621765, 0.6701570749282837, 0.6685959696769714, 0.6622036695480347, 0.6635299324989319, 0.6531742811203003, 0.6307110786437988, 0.6533384323120117, 0.6126009821891785, 0.6299415826797485, 0.6319414377212524, 0.6378813982009888, 0.6902629137039185, 0.6803276538848877, 0.6668713688850403, 0.6676977872848511, 0.6893936395645142, 0.6893426179885864, 0.7384554743766785, 0.752570629119873, 0.7642256617546082, 0.7995278239250183, 0.8179457187652588, 0.8359229564666748, 0.8535662889480591, 0.6376621723175049], "answer_removed_cosine_by_layer": [1.0, 0.999967634677887, 0.9999181032180786, 0.9997936487197876, 0.9997285604476929, 0.9994593262672424, 0.9993605613708496, 0.9990965723991394, 0.9989503622055054, 0.9990646243095398, 0.9989200234413147, 0.9989516735076904, 0.9989333748817444, 0.9985145330429077, 0.998515248298645, 0.9974849224090576, 0.9973975419998169, 0.9961039423942566, 0.9960250854492188, 0.9968388080596924, 0.9968265295028687, 0.9970195889472961, 0.9972777366638184, 0.9975547790527344, 0.99