8e-08, 3.212582555534027e-08]], "new_cot": "1. We know that water, ice, and steam are all different states of the same substance, H2O.\n2. The temperature of a substance is a measure of the average kinetic energy of its particles.\n3. In the solid state (ice), the particles are closely packed and vibrate in place.\n4. In the liquid state (water), the particles are still close together but can move around each other.\n5. In the gaseous state (steam), the particles are far apart and move freely.", "new_cot_probs": [0.00013503452646546066, 1.5810915954261873e-07, 1.5810915954261873e-07, 1.1453389348048404e-08], "cot_prob": [-0.6429214477539062], "cot_step_prob": [-1.3741236925125122], "mechanistic_diagnostics": {"prompt_lengths": {"answer_prompt_tokens": 219, "removed_answer_prompt_tokens": 186, "step_token_count": 37}, "representation": {"step_answer_cosine_by_layer": [0.11630669236183167, 0.8774990439414978, 0.7956176996231079, 0.7599372863769531, 0.7101224064826965, 0.70415198802948, 0.6617357134819031, 0.6556862592697144, 0.6831519603729248, 0.6669211983680725, 0.658045768737793, 0.6421635746955872, 0.6272772550582886, 0.604570209980011, 0.6376621723175049, 0.5906770825386047, 0.5840632915496826, 0.5728232264518738, 0.5781375169754028, 0.6294415593147278, 0.5937846302986145, 0.6067841053009033, 0.6139813661575317, 0.6328150629997253, 0.6209394931793213, 0.6809301376342773, 0.7061964273452759, 0.7136507630348206, 0.7659069299697876, 0.7863617539405823, 0.7992008924484253, 0.8223811388015747, 0.7079189419746399], "answer_removed_cosine_by_layer": [1.0, 0.9999284744262695, 0.9997985363006592, 0.9996023178100586, 0.9995848536491394, 0.9990705251693726, 0.9989281892776489, 0.9987960457801819, 0.9986475706100464, 0.9984837770462036, 0.9982501268386841, 0.9978440403938293, 0.9982730150222778, 0.9976827502250671, 0.9978006482124329, 0.9973052740097046, 0.9966645240783691, 0.9937378764152527, 0.9929537773132324, 0.9942389726638794, 0.9949266910552979, 0.9951996803283691, 0.