 reproduction is the replication of DNA (B).\n5. The next step in both organisms is the division of cells (A).\n6. However, the formation of a cell plate (C) and separation of chromatids (D) are specific to plant cells and some algae during cytokinesis.\n7. Volvox is a green alga, which means it has chloroplasts and is more similar to plant cells than amoebas.\n8. Therefore, the step that you would expect to find in volvox but not in amoebas is the formation of a cell plate (C).", "new_cot_probs": [5.600656827198236e-09, 1.8182669814237329e-09, 1.8918277419288643e-05, 2.3347010991159323e-09], "cot_prob": [-0.3687911629676819], "cot_step_prob": [-0.6806154847145081], "mechanistic_diagnostics": {"prompt_lengths": {"answer_prompt_tokens": 310, "removed_answer_prompt_tokens": 301, "step_token_count": 15}, "representation": {"step_answer_cosine_by_layer": [0.23498037457466125, 0.8831150531768799, 0.809666097164154, 0.7915806174278259, 0.747428834438324, 0.7372622489929199, 0.6879303455352783, 0.6787506937980652, 0.7091822028160095, 0.6993119716644287, 0.6987183690071106, 0.7008410692214966, 0.686648964881897, 0.6598689556121826, 0.6827827095985413, 0.6515848636627197, 0.6517857909202576, 0.6658469438552856, 0.6650434732437134, 0.708116888999939, 0.6976118683815002, 0.6933491230010986, 0.6875840425491333, 0.7150865197181702, 0.7193941473960876, 0.770171046257019, 0.7830334901809692, 0.7783440947532654, 0.8183751106262207, 0.826439380645752, 0.8461185693740845, 0.8618929982185364, 0.7087832093238831], "answer_removed_cosine_by_layer": [1.0, 0.9999796152114868, 0.9999358654022217, 0.999737024307251, 0.9997169375419617, 0.999603271484375, 0.999553382396698, 0.9993517994880676, 0.9992285966873169, 0.9991908073425293, 0.9990934133529663, 0.9987249374389648, 0.998684823513031, 0.9983264803886414, 0.998354971408844, 0.9970377683639526, 0.9966284036636353, 0.9954882860183716, 0.9949249029159546, 0.9960833787918091, 0.9962616562843323, 0.9962061643600464, 0.9964806437492371, 0.996