{"id": "Mercury_7201740", "question": "Giselle makes a model, using foam balls, to represent the events in a solar eclipse. To demonstrate this phenomenon best, the foam ball model should have which characteristic?", "step_idx": 9, "options": ["A): the ability to revolve around the central ball", "B): a magnet in each ball", "C): a representation of oceans on each ball", "D): a source of thermal energy"], "correct": "A", "initial_cot": "1. A solar eclipse occurs when the Moon passes between the Sun and the Earth, blocking the Sun's light from reaching the Earth.\n2. To represent this phenomenon, we need to show the relative positions and movements of the Sun, Moon, and Earth.\n3. The Sun should be the central ball, as it is the largest and most important object in this scenario.\n4. The Earth should be a smaller ball, as it is much smaller than the Sun and the Moon.\n5. The Moon should be an even smaller ball, as it is smaller than both the Sun and the Earth.\n6. The Moon should be able to move around the Earth, as it orbits the Earth in a counterclockwise direction.\n7. The Earth should be able to rotate on its axis, as it rotates from west to east.\n8. The Sun should emit light, as it is the source of light in this scenario.", "initial_cot_probs": [2.133871748810634e-05, 5.289339455316622e-08, 2.83117920218956e-08, 1.0415326379131784e-08], "initial_probs": [0.00020121564739383757, 1.7408565327059478e-06, 6.40425355413754e-07, 4.401574074108794e-07], "prediction": 0, "cot_prediction": 0, "adapter_id": "Mercury_7201740_step_9", "global_job_index": 1225, "cot_step": "The Moon should be an even smaller ball, as it is smaller than both the Sun and the Earth.", "segmented_cot": ["1.", "A solar eclipse occurs when the Moon passes between the Sun and the Earth, blocking the Sun's light from reaching the Earth.", "2.", "To represent this phenomenon, we need to show the relative positions and movements of the Sun, Moon, and Earth.", "3.", "The Sun should be the central ball, as it is the largest and most important object in this scenario.", "4.", "The Earth should be a smaller ball, as it is much smaller than the Sun and the Moon.", "5.", "The Moon should be an even smaller ball, as it is smaller than both the Sun and the Earth.", "6.", "The Moon should be able to move around the Earth, as it orbits the Earth in a counterclockwise direction.", "7.", "The Earth should be able to rotate on its axis, as it rotates from west to east.", "8.", "The Sun should emit light, as it is the source of light in this scenario."], "causal_cot": {"loss": "frodo_reasoning_module", "answer_source": "correct", "counterfactual": "remove_step", "lambda": 0.1, "margin": 1.0, "ie_lambda": 1.0, "margin_lambda": 1.0, "auto_scale": true}, "adapter_record": {"base_model_id": "microsoft/Phi-3-mini-4k-instruct", "adapter_id": "Mercury_7201740_step_9", "adapter_path": "../../../../adapters/arc-challenge/Phi-3/npo_KL_sentencize_s=True_lr=0.0005_rs=1001_pos=True_ff2=False_critical_lora_causal_cot_i09_unfiltered_pos_s1/Mercury_7201740_step_9.pt", "metadata": {"base_model_id": "microsoft/Phi-3-mini-4k-instruct", "dataset": "arc-challenge", "strategy": "sentencize", "stepwise": true, "method": "npo_KL", "instance_id": "Mercury_7201740", "step_idx": 9, "target_index": 157, "global_job_index": 1225, "question": "Giselle makes a model, using foam balls, to represent the events in a solar eclipse. To demonstrate this phenomenon best, the foam ball model should have which characteristic?", "causal_cot": {"loss": "frodo_reasoning_module", "answer_source": "correct", "counterfactual": "remove_step", "lambda": 0.1, "margin": 1.0, "ie_lambda": 1.0, "margin_lambda": 1.0, "auto_scale": true}}}, "adapter_record_path": "v2_outputs/adapter_records/arc-challenge/Phi-3/npo_KL_sentencize_s=True_lr=0.0005_rs=1001_pos=True_ff2=False_critical_lora_causal_cot_i09_unfiltered_pos_s1/Mercury_7201740_step_9.json", "adapter_training_history": [{"epoch": 1, "mean_loss": 15.249238014221191, "evalua