ox is a colonial green alga that reproduces asexually through a process called binary fission.\n3.\nAmoebas are single-celled organisms that also reproduce asexually through binary fission.\n4.\nIn both volvox and amoebas, the first step in asexual reproduction is the replication of DNA (B).\n5.\nThe next step in both organisms is the division of cells (A).\n6.\nHowever, the formation of a cell plate (C) and separation of chromatids (D) are specific to plant cells and some algae during cytokinesis.\n7.", "specificity_preds": [1, 2, 0, 2, 0, 2, 0, 2, 2, 0, 0, 1, 2, 0, 3, 0, 1, 0, 3, 1], "specificity_probs": [[1.6046913797751472e-09, 1.473427164455643e-05, 1.6046913797751472e-09, 1.8183535788196536e-09], [6.810147823443913e-08, 7.716908356769636e-08, 9.589402179699391e-05, 8.744402890670244e-08], [7.877452844695654e-06, 1.7231860383049025e-08, 2.6425912569294496e-09, 5.896417798467724e-10], [5.429062355233327e-08, 5.537794095289428e-06, 4.091907248948701e-05, 1.302364296407177e-07], [2.7457846954348497e-05, 3.643053148039144e-08, 8.128750117464278e-09, 3.643053148039144e-08], [2.0717644133583235e-07, 3.0143993967612914e-07, 2.1132571419002488e-05, 2.474369686922273e-08], [1.8402672139927745e-05, 1.8041346550035087e-07, 4.90414606701961e-07, 5.8571675509710985e-08], [1.953078765382088e-08, 3.220082689381343e-08, 4.534213803708553e-05, 3.220082689381343e-08], [7.70111441283916e-08, 6.117752946011024e-06, 4.520441871136427e-05, 6.796209106596507e-08], [5.58547253604047e-05, 7.031072755125933e-07, 7.967248620843748e-07, 1.4884781194268726e-06], [1.150005391536979e-05, 6.9751358751091175e-06, 6.155536084406776e-06, 2.5660092433099635e-06], [7.306668521778192e-06, 7.855409785406664e-05, 4.764546247315593e-05, 7.306668521778192e-06], [2.4823926025874243e-08, 2.668823526619235e-07, 5.7630546507425606e-05, 4.986019348507398e-07], [3.499446393107064e-05, 3.887533353008621e-07, 2.1931963800625454e-08, 3.615969390580176e-08], [1.952359163226447e-08, 1.2730980358810484e-07, 1.7229