leys.\n2.\nWe need to identify the factor that most likely accounts for this high productivity.\n3.\nThe options given are leaching of soils, evaporation rates, runoff from rains, and amounts of sunlight.\n4.\nLeaching of soils refers to the loss of nutrients from the soil due to water movement.\nThis would likely decrease productivity.\n5.\nEvaporation rates refer to the amount of water that evaporates from the soil and plants.\nHigher evaporation rates can lead to water stress and lower productivity.\n6.\nRunoff from rains refers to the movement of water across the land surface.\nThis can lead to soil erosion and nutrient loss, which would decrease productivity.\n7.\nAmounts of sunlight refer to the amount of solar radiation that reaches the plants.", "specificity_preds": [1, 2, 0, 2, 0, 2, 0, 2, 2, 0, 0, 1, 2, 0, 3, 0, 1, 0, 3, 1], "specificity_probs": [[7.721182271325233e-08, 0.00015819007239770144, 7.721182271325233e-08, 1.1234254060354942e-07], [8.265286055575416e-07, 1.5441588629983016e-06, 0.0005497586098499596, 1.2025921023450792e-06], [9.573354327585548e-05, 5.023634912504349e-07, 4.672708797670566e-08, 1.1814456968295417e-08], [4.3932800508628134e-07, 4.4812677515437827e-05, 0.00022757751867175102, 3.2462191938975593e-06], [0.00026015087496489286, 5.022093887419032e-07, 9.889088659065237e-08, 4.4319816083771e-07], [8.639824045530986e-06, 6.728701464453479e-06, 0.00025249263853766024, 7.091999236763513e-07], [0.00032642806763760746, 3.2001880754251033e-06, 5.978738499834435e-06, 1.1772833659051685e-06], [1.8505031107451941e-07, 2.6924658413918223e-07, 0.00033457876997999847, 3.917514561635471e-07], [1.2010212913082796e-06, 5.1068724133074284e-05, 0.00037734967190772295, 1.5421419448102824e-06], [0.0006660129874944687, 1.3822658729623072e-05, 9.500165106146596e-06, 2.011185097217094e-05], [0.00017572047363501042, 8.300447370857e-05, 7.325119076995179e-05, 3.920853851013817e-05], [5.437040454125963e-05, 0.00040174595778808, 0.00021503913740161806, 4.79817208