 that it has a positive effect on crop growth and yield.\n4. The question provides four possible factors: leaching of soils, evaporation rates, runoff from rains, and amounts of sunlight.\n5. We need to determine which factor most likely has a positive effect on crop growth and yield.\n6. Leaching of soils and evaporation rates are generally negative effects on crop growth and yield, as they can lead to nutrient loss and water loss.\n7. Runoff from rains can have both positive and negative effects on crop growth and yield, depending on the amount and timing of the runoff.\n8. Amounts of sunlight are generally positive effects on crop growth and yield, as they provide energy for photosynthesis and plant development.\n9. Therefore, the increase in amounts of sunlight most likely accounts for the high productivity of some areas in mountain valleys.", "new_cot_probs": [1.0256671900688019e-10, 1.9161987274696202e-10, 1.691039391849003e-10, 5.712107622457552e-07], "cot_prob": [-0.6047176718711853], "cot_step_prob": [-2.903740882873535], "mechanistic_diagnostics": {"prompt_lengths": {"answer_prompt_tokens": 392, "removed_answer_prompt_tokens": 372, "step_token_count": 32}, "representation": {"step_answer_cosine_by_layer": [0.14927002787590027, 0.8722779154777527, 0.7958947420120239, 0.7811911702156067, 0.7464202642440796, 0.7514017820358276, 0.715622067451477, 0.7188740968704224, 0.7548627853393555, 0.7569129467010498, 0.7638436555862427, 0.752090573310852, 0.7338475584983826, 0.7303422689437866, 0.7486209869384766, 0.7102261185646057, 0.717234194278717, 0.7118751406669617, 0.701783299446106, 0.7477872967720032, 0.7343917489051819, 0.7131277322769165, 0.6913554668426514, 0.7041081190109253, 0.7116762399673462, 0.7607651352882385, 0.7666175365447998, 0.7496111392974854, 0.8011858463287354, 0.8095811605453491, 0.8283741474151611, 0.8452787399291992, 0.6910926103591919], "answer_removed_cosine_by_layer": [1.0, 0.9999308586120605, 0.9998200535774231, 0.9979311227798462, 0.9973