d buoyancy of the boats.\n3.\nOption (A) suggests constructing a prototype of a boat for testing.\nThis would allow the students to observe how the boat behaves in water and make necessary adjustments to improve its stability and buoyancy.\n4.\nOption (B) involves calculating the total mass of all the finished boats.\nWhile this information might be useful for other purposes, it doesn't directly address the issue of stability and buoyancy.\n5.\nOption (C) suggests determining the total amount of weight each boat can carry.\nThis is related to the boat's capacity, but it doesn't directly address the issue of stability and buoyancy.\n6.\nOption (D) involves testing the strength of each material used to construct the boats.", "specificity_preds": [1, 2, 0, 2, 0, 2, 0, 2, 2, 0, 0, 1, 2, 0, 3, 0, 1, 0, 3, 1], "specificity_probs": [[7.721182271325233e-08, 0.00015819007239770144, 7.721182271325233e-08, 1.1234254060354942e-07], [8.265286055575416e-07, 1.5441588629983016e-06, 0.0005497586098499596, 1.2025921023450792e-06], [9.573354327585548e-05, 5.023634912504349e-07, 4.672708797670566e-08, 1.1814456968295417e-08], [4.3932800508628134e-07, 4.4812677515437827e-05, 0.00022757751867175102, 3.2462191938975593e-06], [0.00026015087496489286, 5.022093887419032e-07, 9.889088659065237e-08, 4.4319816083771e-07], [8.639824045530986e-06, 6.728701464453479e-06, 0.00025249263853766024, 7.091999236763513e-07], [0.00032642806763760746, 3.2001880754251033e-06, 5.978738499834435e-06, 1.1772833659051685e-06], [1.8505031107451941e-07, 2.6924658413918223e-07, 0.00033457876997999847, 3.917514561635471e-07], [1.2010212913082796e-06, 5.1068724133074284e-05, 0.00037734967190772295, 1.5421419448102824e-06], [0.0006660129874944687, 1.3822658729623072e-05, 9.500165106146596e-06, 2.011185097217094e-05], [0.00017572047363501042, 8.300447370857e-05, 7.325119076995179e-05, 3.920853851013817e-05], [5.437040454125963e-05, 0.00040174595778808, 0.00021503913740161806, 4.798172085429542e-05], [4.93419975100550